# ADR-000: Bootstrap

## Status

Accepted on bootstrap.

## Context

`{{ project_name }}` was created from the `library-typescript` Copier template at `ika100/sdlc-foundry`. The template encodes the platform's TypeScript library conventions (platform ADR-124 for the tooling, ADR-125 for publishing):

- Node {{ node_major }} LTS and pnpm via devbox; ESM only, TypeScript strict, compiled with `tsc` to `dist/` with type declarations
- ESLint (typescript-eslint) + `tsc --noEmit` as the quality gate; `pnpm audit` and detect-secrets for security
- Vitest with an 80 % coverage gate
- The npm package `@{{ github_org | lower }}/{{ project_name }}`, published to GitHub Packages by the `publish` CI job of a `v*` tag; the tag is the version
- No server, no container image, no Kubernetes
- Claude Code agents from the `sdlc-foundry` marketplace (`svc-ts` + `svc` + `shared`)

## Decision

We adopt the platform conventions verbatim. Any deviation must be justified in a new ADR.

## Consequences

Skeleton updates (CI, devbox recipes, the publish script, Node bump, lint and test config) arrive through `copier update`; `src/`, `tests/`, `package.json` and `docs/adr/` are project-owned and never overwritten.
